# Security and authorization

Follow `docs/project/CONSTITUTION.md` §§7, 13. Admin `/admin/*` routes use Spatie `permission:` middleware from `config/acl.php`. Vue `usePermission` / `useNavigation` remain UX only. See Foundation Backlog for unused ACL groups and deferred `MustVerifyEmail`.

## Non-negotiable

**Frontend permission visibility is not authorization.** Protected operations MUST be authorized server-side (`authorize()`, `can:` middleware, policies once adopted, or equivalent) before mutating or returning sensitive data.

New AB2TI modules MUST declare which permissions/roles gate which operations. Add permissions in `config/acl.php` and sync with `acl:sync` — never Vue-only strings.

## MUST NOT silently change

Public registration, `MustVerifyEmail`, Fortify/Jetstream feature flags, or `Gate::before` super-admin behavior. Those are product/security decisions.

## Request and data safety

Validate writes. Mass-assign only `$fillable` / validated arrays — not `$request->all()` onto models. Restrict upload MIME/size. Public CMS/language/catch-all endpoints MUST NOT leak admin data.

Never commit `.env` or secrets. Never print secret values in reports. No `dd()` / `dump()` / debug PHP in completed work.
